  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Psycho-Emotional Care for Children and Adolescents in Situations of Mobility in Uruguay</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The migratory experience is often treated as a phenomenon in which children and adolescents are passive actors in migration and only accompany adults on human mobility routes. In this way, assistance programs usually focus on general difficulties manifested in the adult universe of migrants and would be &#x201c;replicated&#x201d; in the reality of childhood. However, during a previous collaboration experience between IOM, the organization Idas y Vuelva and UNICEF, the relevance of improving the availability and quality of psycho-emotional support with a focus on children and adolescents was made visible. This project aims to provide psycho-emotional and social support focused on migrant children and adolescents and generate knowledge that guides the best ways to contribute to healthy psycho-emotional development during the migration process.</narrative>
  </description>
